    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for June 11, 2026, centers on the high-upside pairing of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker**. **Gunnar Henderson** (75.30) stands as our premier play, benefiting from a favorable 16% park factor bump and a significant dynamic platoon advantage against Bryan Woo. While Woo\u2019s stuff is notable, the combination of **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s aggressive approach and the park-adjusted ceiling makes him our clear anchor. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (68.96) provides a high-floor, high-ceiling option against Mitch Keller; despite hitting lower in the order, his intrinsic talent and the favorable platoon profile make him a core contributor today, even with the looming weather concerns in Pittsburgh.\n\nWe are navigating a few situational risks as we finalize the lineup. **Josh Jung** (63.50) carries a strong score bolstered by a 10% wind-out factor at the stadium, but he\u2014along with **Andy Pages** (63.73)\u2014is subject to a moderate rain risk (30\u201338%), which necessitates keeping a close eye on pre-game alerts. The most difficult bench decision involved **Liam Hicks** (57.76) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.80); both sit just outside the \"Strong\" start threshold (60+). **Liam Hicks** is being leaned on for his lead-off spot, which grants him a 10% order bonus, but his base projection remains modest. Ultimately, we are keeping **Coby Mayo** (44.47) in the UTIL slot to capture his park-adjusted power potential against Bryan Woo, though his dynamic platoon handicap (\u20138%) makes him the most vulnerable member of our starting nine. \n\nWith **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remaining sidelined on the IL, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** enjoying an off-day, our depth is being tested. We are leaning heavily into the speed and efficiency profile of **Sam Antonacci** (54.21) despite his L/L platoon disadvantage against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, as our 5x5 Roto strategy necessitates prioritize SB-capable bats even when the matchup efficiency metrics are slightly suppressed. We will continue to monitor the status of **Dominic Smith** and **Coby Mayo** as lineups finalize to ensure no late-scratch scenarios necessitate a rotation from our remaining reserves.",
